[
  {"id": "gold-promotions", "request": "Add `addGoldPromotion(d, sku, minQuantity, percent)`, with the same checks and result as `addPromotion`, for promotions that only gold customers get. A gold customer's line gets the best percent among the sku's general and gold promotions it qualifies for; other customers' lines get only general promotions. The gold discount (`GOLD_PERCENT`) still applies to the order's amount afterwards. `lineCents(d, entry)` keeps its parameters and prices the line for a customer who is not gold."},
  {"id": "platinum-tier", "request": "Add a customer tier \"platinum\": its orders get 5% off their amount instead of the gold 3%, and its lines get every promotion a gold customer's would. Add `addPlatinumCustomer(d, id, name, creditCents)` with the same checks and result as `addCustomer`, and `tierOf(d, id)` returning \"regular\", \"gold\" or \"platinum\", or \"\" for an unknown customer."},
  {"id": "hold-review", "request": "Add a second threshold: an order whose amount (`orderCents`) is 500000 cents or more is held for review when placed, even within the customer's credit: `statusOf` says \"onHold\", it reserves its stock and is logged \"held ID\" like any held order, and it opens review work \"review:ID\" instead of credit work. Payments and cancellations never release an order held for review. Add `approve(d, id)` returning `Result<Depot, string>`, which fails unless the order is held for review. Approving logs \"approved ID\", closes its review work, and then checks the order's credit as when it was placed (its own amount counted once): within credit it becomes placed and is logged \"placed ID\" without opening review work again; over credit it becomes held for credit, logged \"held ID\" with credit work for the customer, and is released by payments like any order held for credit. Placed orders from `REVIEW_CENTS` (200000) up to 500000 keep opening review work as they do now."},
  {"id": "partial-pay", "request": "Add `payPart(d, number, cents)` returning `Result<Depot, string>`: it pays `cents` of an unpaid invoice, failing for an unknown or paid invoice or for cents that are not positive or more than is still due. The customer owes that much less, and the payment is logged \"paid NUMBER\" and releases held orders like a full payment. An invoice is paid once nothing is due on it. `pay` pays whatever is still due. In `statement`, a partly paid invoice's line ends with \"due\" and the cents still due, as \"#2 5 10000 due 4000\"; other lines do not change."},
  {"id": "return-goods", "request": "Add `returnGoods(d, id, sku, quantity)` returning `Result<Depot, string>` for a shipped order. The units go back to the order's location as a stock change, and the customer is credited what the order's amount (with today's prices, promotions and tier) drops by when those units leave the line. The credit is a new invoice for the order with that amount negated, already paid; the customer owes that much less, and it releases held orders like a payment. After the stock change it is logged \"returned ID SKU QUANTITY\". It fails for an unknown or unshipped order, a sku not in the order, a quantity that is not positive, or more units than the line has left after earlier returns. `orderCents` of the order does not change."},
  {"id": "reorder-per-location", "request": "Add `setReorder(d, sku, location, level)` returning `Result<Depot, string>`, failing for an unknown sku, an empty location or a negative level; setting it again replaces the level. While a location has a level for a sku, its quantity at or below the level keeps one open reorder work \"reorder:SKU@LOCATION\", closed when the quantity rises above it. Setting a level applies this rule at once, without a log line. The item-wide rule on the total stock stays as it is, and log lines do not change."},
  {"id": "change-line", "request": "Add `changeLine(d, id, sku, quantity)` returning `Result<Depot, string>` for a placed or held order: it sets the quantity of the order's line for a known `sku`, adding the line at the end when the order has none and removing it at 0. The difference is reserved from or returned to the order's location as stock changes; when the location lacks the units, it fails and nothing changes. An order left with no lines is cancelled as by `cancel`. Otherwise the credit check runs again as when placed, with the order's new amount counted once: a placed order over credit becomes held for credit (logged \"held ID\", with credit work), and an order held for credit that now fits becomes placed (logged \"placed ID\", closing the customer's credit work when none of its orders is still held for credit). An order held for review stays held for review. A quantity below 0 fails."},
  {"id": "rename-customer", "request": "Rename the field `customer` of `Order` and of `Invoice` to `customerId` everywhere."}
]
